    "title": "Hired painter pleads guilty to raping 11-year-old girl in Peekskill: DA - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ben Mitchell ,\n2 hours ago\nWHITE PLAINS, N.Y. (PIX11) — A 60-year-old man pleaded guilty to raping an 11-year-old girl in 2024 in Peekskill, Westchester County District Attorney Susan Cacace announced Wednesday.\nThe defendant, Anselmo Yambay Pena, was hired to paint apartments at a residential building in Peekskill, prosecutors say.\nMore Local News The incident happened in an apartment on Feb. 15, 2024.\n“I can only imagine the grief and horror experienced by the victim in this case because of this defendant’s depravity,” DA Cacace said. “A guilty plea now provides her and her family with finality, without having to subject her to the difficult process of trial preparation. I am humbled by her courage and resilience in the face of this disturbing abuse, and my office will continue to provide her with supportive services.”\nPena was promised a sentence of 17 years in state prison. Sentencing is scheduled for Oct. 7.\nBen Mitchell is a digital content producer from Vermont who has covered both local and international news since 2021. He joined PIX11 in 2024. See more of his work here .\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to PIX11.",
